# SCP system environment configuration template.
#
# Copy to .env and edit values for your deployment:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file is the DOCUMENTED contract for env vars that the SCP system
# reads. The runtime contract is the real .env. They must stay in sync.
#
# Phase 7-A fixes (Root Cause 7 — Hardcoded paths/ports/numbers không validate):
#   - Fix 4-d-015: SCP_INTERNAL_URL + LOOP_SCHEDULER_URL documented here.
#     Dashboard API routes (dashboard/src/app/api/scp/*) probe these URLs to
#     build the composite health status. If absent, they silently fall back
#     to localhost defaults — works locally but FAILS SILENTLY in container /
#     split-deploy scenarios. Set explicitly for any non-default deployment.
#   - Fix 4-d-016: 6 OPENROUTER_MODEL_* keys documented here. Phase 3-B fix
#     4-d-005 wired these env vars into the llm-bridge's TASK_MODEL_MAP — but
#     the .env.example template never listed them. New deployers silently lost
#     per-task model routing (all tasks fell back to a single OPENROUTER_MODEL).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Internal service URLs (Fix 4-d-015)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard API routes read these to build the composite health status
# (dashboard/src/app/api/scp/health/route.ts). All three services are probed
# in parallel — if any is unreachable, the dashboard shows "degraded" or
# "offline". Without these env vars the dashboard silently uses localhost
# defaults; operators only notice when the deploy is non-local.
#
# Consumers:
#   - SCP_INTERNAL_URL:        health/route.ts, status/route.ts, scanners/route.ts, autofix/route.ts
#   - LOOP_SCHEDULER_URL:     health/route.ts, loop/route.ts, loop/trigger/route.ts
#   - LLM_BRIDGE_URL:         health/route.ts (third sibling URL — same pattern)
SCP_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8002
LOOP_SCHEDULER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3030
LLM_BRIDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# SCP backend root path (used by status/route.ts to compute live v4 LOC).
# Optional: when dashboard runs from this repository, the route resolves the
# repository root from its working directory. Set an absolute path only when
# dashboard and backend are deployed separately.
# SCP_ROOT=C:\\path\\to\\GA-LAB

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-task model routing (Fix 4-d-016)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Phase 3-B fix 4-d-005 wired these env vars into the llm-bridge's
# TASK_MODEL_MAP (mini-services/llm-bridge/index.ts:131-143). SCP sends
# task-specific model names ("autofix", "chat", "judge", "learning",
# "fast_learning", "why" — and their ":8b" / ":7b" aliases) and the bridge
# maps them to these OpenRouter model IDs.
#
# If a key is absent, the bridge falls back to OPENROUTER_MODEL (single
# model for everything) — silently losing per-task routing. All 6 should be
# set for any deploy that uses OpenRouter (vs local Ollama).
#
# Default model IDs below are conservative free-tier picks; tune for your
# OpenRouter subscription / quality requirements.
OPENROUTER_MODEL_AUTOFIX=deepseek/deepseek-r1:8b
OPENROUTER_MODEL_CHAT=meta-llama/llama-3.2-3b-instruct
OPENROUTER_MODEL_JUDGE=qwen/qwen2.5-7b-instruct
OPENROUTER_MODEL_LEARNING=qwen/qwen2.5-7b-instruct
OPENROUTER_MODEL_FAST_LEARNING=meta-llama/llama-3.2-3b-instruct
OPENROUTER_MODEL_WHY=qwen/qwen2.5-7b-instruct

# Fallback model (used when none of the per-task keys match, or for general
# requests that don't carry a task-specific model name).
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free
